  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a maintainer, I want the image and video halves of the `LOT-003-settings` legacy oracles compared by a suite, so that the M4 parity of the image and video settings is checked against legacy and not only asserted.\n\n### Scope\n\n- LOT-070's gate A (PR #930) found that the image and video halves of the `LOT-003-settings` oracles are compared by no suite. The specs of LOT-107 and LOT-108 now say so, but no issue tracked it.\n- Add the differential comparison for those halves, in the suite that owns the settings, or pin each difference as a documented deviation. `OracleOwnershipTests` (#930) must still pass.\n\n### Sources\n\n- The gate A table in `docs/lots/LOT-070-*.md` (#930), and the LOT-107 and LOT-108 specs.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every image and video field of the `LOT-003-settings` oracles is compared, or pinned with its reason.\n- [ ] A test fails when one of those fields changes.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
